    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f595edf3-44be-5e81-9dc8-1d526befbd8d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{4}$ given that  $6a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-2x & =b \\\\ -2x & =b-6a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(b-6a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-6\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}-{x}_{4}=7-1=6.$",
